From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:14:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: Add MT6789 stateless H.264 video decoder driver

Add a firmware-free V4L2 stateless M2M H.264 video decoder driver
(mtk-vdec-mt6789) for the MediaTek MT6789 (Helio G99) single-core VDEC
hardware block.

Instead of relying on the closed-source Android userspace VCU/vpud stack
or ChromeOS SCP firmware, the driver programs the VLD, VLDTOP, MC,
AVCVLD, AVCMV, PP, and MISC MMIO blocks directly:
- Exposes V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264_SLICE (Annex-B, frame-based, Media Request
  API) on OUTPUT_MPLANE and V4L2_PIX_FMT_MM21 (2-plane 16x32 block NV12)
  on CAPTURE_MPLANE.
- Sets a 34-bit DMA mask when IOMMU-mapped so disp_iommu can allocate
  IOVAs in SMI LARB4 Region 1 (4 GiB..8 GiB), stripping bank bit 32
  before shifted hardware address fields.
- Uses the AVCVLD hardware barrel shifter and reordering/weight-table
  engines for slice header parsing and triggers GIC SPI 458 completion.

Signed-off-by: sysretq0 <sysretq0@proton.me>
---
